<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:29:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Russia and Ukraine trade blame for cyber attacks as fragile ceasefire ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39ee6dadebf367b423b28df0cacc8a50111853beb667aa2fb29ab0c8bc3c36b7</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T06:19:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-live-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-cyber-attacks-fragile-ceasefire-ends--a26586664aa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-live-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-cyber-attacks-fragile-ceasefire-ends" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine on Monday traded accusations over cyberattacks, with Moscow reporting a hack of its emergency alerts app hours after Kyiv said its own air raid warning system had been compromised. The incidents came as a fragile ceasefire in Ukraine's Kherson region expired, raising fears of renewed fighting. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine accuse each other of hacking emergency alert apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4019a14ea52a0dd2cec777cf23a5811c6f09463467dda37c4f34054837991f1</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T01:20:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-ukraine-suspects-nationwide-air-raid-alert-app-has-been-hacked--083a045e3724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-ukraine-suspects-nationwide-air-raid-alert-app-has-been-hacked" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine accused each other of hacking their emergency alert applications as a local ceasefire in the war's eastern Kherson region expired on Sunday. The cyberattacks came as both sides warned of renewed fighting and Kyiv signalled it could halt strikes on Russian oil refineries in exchange for US Patriot missiles.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland rocked by Constitutional showdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63266d2b9b90c230c82572683cf895fd9f82ba1591a90dde4d8026a1e5c66caf</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:41:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown--f25dbb628a78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown" /><summary type="html">Poland’s constitutional crisis deepened on Saturday as the European Commission urged President Karol Nawrocki to recognise new judges appointed by Prime Minister Donald Tusk. The standoff comes ahead of next year’s parliamentary election, with polls suggesting a close race between Tusk’s coalition and the nationalist right. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ceasefire in Ukraine's Kherson region ends after Russia refuses extension</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de3452343444ab3012569ac62b0985a8108e4fcea2063e95a9fe2bea7c47c083</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:29:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T12:41:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-localised-ceasefire-in-ukraine-s-kherson-region-set-to-end--ecd92f33424f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-localised-ceasefire-in-ukraine-s-kherson-region-set-to-end" /><summary type="html">The longest truce of the war in Ukraine, localised in the region of Kherson, ended on Sunday after Russia refused to extend the ceasefire. The temporary pause in fighting, which began on Tuesday, enabled a humanitarian mission to the Russian-occupied town of Olechky.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Lula's victory, Israeli elections and Spain train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:184202b91db2507138aa803be1e2a0a6f5bd012a4b6b91943ebb633f25b422a4</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T11:14:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash--07ac9159f69c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash" /><summary type="html">From Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's reelection in Brazil's presidential polls, to razor-sharp margins in the Israeli general elections, to a deadly high-speed train collision in Spain, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Youth-led rallies sweep Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82cf48db68af6dc5cba87fc6e5fcf0469ac44423e6cf509005ccd3df2aae7a7a</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe--7747234b0c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe" /><summary type="html">Protests in France have helped inspire youth demonstrations elsewhere in Europe, from Portugal and Italy to Germany. Germany saw particularly large rallies on Saturday, led by a youth initiative whose name roughly translates as “Gen Z has got this”. Demonstrators called for better education and healthcare, stronger climate protection and a more affordable cost of living, while also opposing any return to compulsory military service. However, protests in several major German cities turned violent towards the end of the day, particularly in the financial hub of Frankfurt. Charlotte Hughes reports on the demonstrations across Europe.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bulgarians vote in presidential runoff amid security tensions in the Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7995247e345e3f08192d86055a1b3ac75fdd3e97f6b3ac8e0d7ba89a96bd8d</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T05:47:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea--8b2d7985fd75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea" /><summary type="html">Bulgarians voted Sunday in a presidential runoff between two candidates with opposing views on the Ukraine war and relations with Russia as tensions mount in the Black Sea. Exit polls showed Bulgaria's incumbent President Iliana Iotova, who favours dialogue with Moscow, led the vote against Andrey Gyurov.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Testimonies from Oleshky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e03fd826f3a7f859fe01a4536bea2ab9ead8176f0657096ebe4e0f4336c8c505</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T23:54:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky--738a0891e290.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky" /><summary type="html">American Filmmaker Zarina Zabrisky has lived and reported across the Dnipro River in Ukrainian controlled Kherson for the past three years. She’s been speaking to France 24’s Gavin Lee about the events of the past 24 hours.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'Gen Z' demonstrations across Germany demand more education funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53502b09fbdec79e07ba16f66c7290612a8d20a11046f35e0c5eff8f4579be88</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T20:07:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos--1625df057110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos" /><summary type="html">Police and protesters clashed Saturday in Germany where tens of thousands of young people took to the streets, inspired by similar movements in other European countries. Organized by the "GenZ regelt!" ("Gen Z has got this!") group, marches were held nationwide to demand more funding for education and to protest the high cost of living.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Residents from Russian-occupied Oleshky reunite with families after evacuation operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7e889e4e6f73bb0c0c5ab2169922b71d97c233f235db61c8d40d8f24c427832</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T12:45:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-evacuees-from-russian-occupied-oleshky-arrive-in-ukraine--53005b26a236.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-evacuees-from-russian-occupied-oleshky-arrive-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Evacuees from Oleshky crossed into Ukrainian-held territory Saturday in a major rescue operation after travelling through Belarus during a rare truce brokered by US First Lady Melania Trump. The city of Oleshky has been under Russian occupation since 2022 and was caught in intense fighting that left residents starving and unable to leave.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham says 'open' to slavery apology but rules out financial reparations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cf1c7b2c5dde2e4b1f3de3be659f1db84b91c79c79459fd03e3461f6a15981b</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T12:31:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-burnham-says-uk-open-to-slavery-apology-but-rules-out-financial-reparations--afe052dbec14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-burnham-says-uk-open-to-slavery-apology-but-rules-out-financial-reparations" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham said Saturday he was "open" to the UK apologising for the first time for its role in the transatlantic slave trade but rejected calls for financial reparations. Issues around Britain's colonial history have loomed large over King Charles' ongoing visit to three Caribbean nations ahead of Commonwealth summit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Protesters gather at Poland's Top court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4358d7c89d05f6bca18f447127ad32f0b8fcdf635351203c3b73382eaa1b916</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:31:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/protesters-gather-at-poland-s-top-court--ffa4a59e5a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/protesters-gather-at-poland-s-top-court" /><summary type="html">Police in Poland have stepped up security around the country’s Constitutional Tribunal after dozens of protesters gathered on Friday to oppose the government’s suspension of its president, which they say was unlawful. Police say several people were detained after some demonstrators breached the court’s perimeter fence. Charlotte Hughes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Polish president holds crisis talks after dramatic court standoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed1b7da373f6756f72a62e7b225846c25c469f90ab336c7a21b8b9ec7da42c03</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T01:27:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-polish-president-holds-crisis-talks-in-court-standoff--d507691b9fab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-polish-president-holds-crisis-talks-in-court-standoff" /><summary type="html">Poland's President Karol Nawrocki held emergency talks with political leaders on Saturday as a bitter dispute over the constitutional court escalated into a crisis over judicial independence. The row over appointing the court's judges pits Prime Minister Donald Tusk's pro-EU government against a nationalist opposition and right-wing president.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Residents leave Russian-occupied Oleshky in evacuation operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3055e0fc281c99edb5abe8fa25d3eccfd75544252fc902a61f411a5473d1400</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T21:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-residents-leave-russian-occupied-oleshky-in-evacuation-operation--14ad8cd95743.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-residents-leave-russian-occupied-oleshky-in-evacuation-operation" /><summary type="html">Residents evacuated from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have left for Russia's Anapa city with a Ukrainian delegation, senior official David Arakhamia said Friday. They are expected to fly to Belarus before returning to Ukraine by bus, during a rare ceasefire brokered by the United States.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Oleshky: No access to basic needs, ceasefire offers limited opportunity for humanitarian assistance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0535c9e0525f4a401b17cc0e718c843cffae69b8aea9abb11ab27fc00a4ae6cc</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T17:11:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/oleshky-no-access-to-basic-needs-ceasefire-offers-limited-opportunity-for-humanitarian-assistance--31d5d457bf7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/oleshky-no-access-to-basic-needs-ceasefire-offers-limited-opportunity-for-humanitarian-assistance" /><summary type="html">Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Jens Schumacher, Field Coordinator in Mykolaiv and Kherson with Solidarity International. Just a few kilometers separate the Ukrainian-controlled city of Kherson from Russian-occupied Oleshky. For civilians caught between military occupation, disrupted essential services and uncertain evacuation arrangements, geographical proximity offers little guarantee of access to life-saving assistance. Schumacher examines the humanitarian implications of a temporary ceasefire around Oleshky, where approximately 2,000 civilians were reported to remain. Although the cessation of attacks has created a limited opportunity for humanitarian operations, the geographical scope of the agreement, the prospects for evacuation and the possibility of sustained humanitarian access remain uncertain.</summary></entry><entry><title>'The International Criminal Court deserves the Sakharov Prize': CJEU President Koen Lenaerts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb1519943ed1097c77f8e00811cd7566bfeb3fe8e6239f1233ea8da69b6f0c99</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:51:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261030-the-international-criminal-court-deserves-the-sakharov-prize-cjeu-president-koen-lenaerts--dc9a3cd2d160.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261030-the-international-criminal-court-deserves-the-sakharov-prize-cjeu-president-koen-lenaerts" /><summary type="html">We speak to the influential and long-serving president of the Court of Justice of the European Union (CJEU), Koen Lenaerts. The court is the EU's supreme judicial authority, responsible for ensuring that European law is interpreted and applied across all 27 member states.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Star Wars: Has Russia's war with Ukraine gone intergalactic?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe43e934224bc88fd09c8bc3697ccd012d1cde23d60bc76ec677b2026fe68e5</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:29:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-star-wars-has-russias-war-with-ukraine-gone-intergalactic--c418152504bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-star-wars-has-russias-war-with-ukraine-gone-intergalactic" /><summary type="html">Russian made an unprecedented combative move this month as one of its military satellites, the Cosmos-2612, encroached upon the orbit of Ukrainian commercial satellite, Iceye-X36, in behaviour deemed "threatening" by the US State Department. Norbert Pouzin, an orbital analyst at French space tech firm, Aldoria, described the mercenary manoeuvre as the first of its kind.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Could US midterms impact the EU? Transatlantic ties hit new low after Trump-Putin diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ed9f22a9248afe0dc6752523dbbd93c183bdd7cbf0caf5f5f9e1ce67f828b10</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:24:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261030-could-us-midterms-impact-the-eu-transatlantic-ties-hit-new-low-after-trump-putin-diesel-dea--7e490da5ab7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261030-could-us-midterms-impact-the-eu-transatlantic-ties-hit-new-low-after-trump-putin-diesel-deal" /><summary type="html">From the EU's perspective, the second Trump presidency has felt even more destabilising than the first. From making the false claim that the EU was set up to "screw" the United States, to slapping tariffs on European goods, to making territorial claims on Greenland, to doing a diesel deal with Vladimir Putin and telling Ukraine to get a new president, Donald Trump has more than ruffled feathers on this side of the ocean. He has shaken the very foundations of the historical transatlantic relationship.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French port strikes: Unions 'will get better working conditions', but can they curb militarisation?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a485d83640223f37b8d087477323e93fc6130eacb6ffb060a750ed97d733a590</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:20:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-french-port-strikes-unions-will-get-better-working-conditions-but-can-they-curb-militarizat--400f47409b4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-french-port-strikes-unions-will-get-better-working-conditions-but-can-they-curb-militarization-1" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Renaud Foucart, Senior Lecturer at the Department of Economics ECARES at Lancaster University. An international dockworkers’ strike brings into focus the relationship between organized labor, technological change and Europe’s expanding military investment. Foucart argues that port workers’ strategic position in global supply chains gives them exceptional leverage: “They know how powerful they are.” While questioning their ability to redirect military policy, he expects that leverage to secure concessions on automation and working conditions: “They can get those concessions. And I think they will get them.”</summary></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Evacuations under way in Russian-occupied Oleshky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ece4209cbaebd61adc530f6d7f7eb4e2e548b211ea1e17ad920d368679a3c806</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:01:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-war-in-ukraine-evacuations-under-way-in-russian-occupied-oleshky--0b50a9aa1fe5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-war-in-ukraine-evacuations-under-way-in-russian-occupied-oleshky" /><summary type="html">Starving and exhausted residents of Oleshky, a Russian-occupied town in southern Ukraine, were being evacuated on Friday, October 30, as part of a joint relief operation involving the opposing sides – the first operation of its kind in four years and eight months of war. FRANCE 24’s Ukraine correspondent Emmanuelle Chaze reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>French crowd gathers for anti-islamophobia rally in Paris suburb after attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea875bf66083e74bb49d20498071b20f7165e25eb9aa74a4e4f8fd09bc1df65a</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-french-crowd-gathers-for-anti-islamophobia-rally-in-paris-suburb-after-attack--9e3dfdb8b766.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-french-crowd-gathers-for-anti-islamophobia-rally-in-paris-suburb-after-attack" /><summary type="html">In France, thousands were protesting in the Paris suburb of La Verrière on Friday, a week after a racist terrorist attack killed one person and injured five others. The suspect, identified as Kevin T., admitted he was targeting people based on their appearance or religion and has been transferred to a Paris court. FRANCE 24's Morgan Ayre reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain working to identify train crash dead as relatives' anguish grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd824ed882cf10a323297a12d36cccdcf04acd2117843e315ec2ed02778c00d4</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:34:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spain-working-to-identify-train-crash-dead-as-relatives-anguish-grows--fb8e5225b2b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spain-working-to-identify-train-crash-dead-as-relatives-anguish-grows" /><summary type="html">A second day of mourning is underway in Spain, with some families still waiting for news about missing loved ones, following Wednesday's high speed train crash that killed 69 people. Some have flooded social media with desperate appeals for information, posting photos or describing the clothes their relatives were wearing when they boarded the trains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Black Sea shipping under growing threats as drones hit container ships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4312374aa0e1bb164428ba5dcff5a1b318ffba8875abe3e6f4c44209d7266b69</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:27:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/black-sea-shipping-under-growing-threats-as-drones-hit-container-ships--cfebd1c5305b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/black-sea-shipping-under-growing-threats-as-drones-hit-container-ships" /><summary type="html">A Greek container ship has sunk after being struck by three drones, potentially of Russian origin, in the Black Sea off the Bulgarian coast on Wednesday, October 28. This incident highlights growing concerns for commercial shipping as the conflict between Ukraine and Russia persists.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spanish transport minister faces calls to quit after deadly train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b73323b28e67f2c350a6ce0617e69abc1f79e6f11e6e023f7ab35a63c13e279a</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:21:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spanish-transport-minister-faces-calls-to-quit-after-deadly-train-crash--f9d11340adfa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spanish-transport-minister-faces-calls-to-quit-after-deadly-train-crash" /><summary type="html">Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente faced calls to resign but ruled out stepping down on Friday. This follows Wednesday’s train crash in Toledo province, which killed 69 people. It is the country’s second high-speed rail disaster this year. FRANCE 24 correspondent Sarah Morris reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Third weekend of protests looms as tensions persist across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d49bfe06a72ed5f297d2da96fdf8544c750c6b6687d45964d402c984daf33480</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:10:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-third-weekend-of-protests-looms-as-tensions-persist-across-france--4d3c0a7cc2ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-third-weekend-of-protests-looms-as-tensions-persist-across-france" /><summary type="html">For the third Saturday in a row, people across France are set to take to the streets to protest against the high cost of living and demand better funding for education. Police are preparing for all eventualities ahead of another weekend of protests, following earlier demonstrations that ended in rioting and looting in city centres.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is Kevin T., the main suspect behind the racist Trappes attack?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c9ef56677537fb86b83cfcdeacff6733091ecfca43fd02c390edf5e8b113258</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-is-kevin-t-the-main-suspect-behind-the-racist-trappes-attack--33783e54c60a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-kevin-t-the-main-suspect-behind-the-racist-trappes-attack" /><summary type="html">France's anti-terrorism prosecutor on Thursday released details of the main suspect in the racist attack in Trappes and La Verriere, on the outskirts of Paris, on October 23.The 39-year-old opened fire with a submachine gun, killing 26-year-old Pengo Bossio Wangi and injuring five others.</summary></entry><entry><title>Georgia's European dream left in limbo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc2ac13ec2cf83e7af00282a77eaa9852d434726ff650e7a33da1e91a3b6597a</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:34:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261030-georgia-s-european-dream-left-in-limbo--4741bd8d840a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261030-georgia-s-european-dream-left-in-limbo" /><summary type="html">Two years ago in Georgia, tens of thousands of pro-European protesters rallied against the disputed results of the October 2024 parliamentary election, which was officially won by the ruling Georgian Dream party. A few weeks later, the authorities announced the suspension of the country's European Union accession process. Despite an ongoing crackdown, smaller-scale protests continue every day in the capital Tbilisi.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fae8b2b3390dd65c3b6b2c2c4f978b8f298755a9f2a0ae7b37722c8d9ea9bc66</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers--daeb7f5e2250.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers" /><summary type="html">While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's bastion of free press Novaya Gazeta shuts down under Kremlin pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83b58273f5f963a18975ebed2213e458817ba3c3d7d581b908d26a7251934684</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:42:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-russia-s-bastion-of-free-press-novaya-gazeta-shuts-down-after-years-of-kremlin-pressure--649e1731fac7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-russia-s-bastion-of-free-press-novaya-gazeta-shuts-down-after-years-of-kremlin-pressure" /><summary type="html">Newspaper Novaya Gazeta, one of the last vestiges of independent journalism in Russia, announced Friday that it was closing down, citing pressure from authorities who recently searched the home of its senior editor and earlier this year detained one of its journalists.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US approves potential sale of 500 Patriot missiles to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:516762a7aae2e14caa2d6c588f0a90022d9dbf8d960694e45755555a62a74861</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:28:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-live-russia-strikes-energy-facilities-kyiv-aid-convoy-heads-besieged-town-oleshky-ukraine--d650042d9ed7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-live-russia-strikes-energy-facilities-kyiv-aid-convoy-heads-besieged-town-oleshky-ukraine" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has approved the sale of 500 Patriot missiles to Ukraine to bolster its air defences, the US State Department said Friday. Meanwhile, evacuees from Russian-occupied Oleshky have begun their journey back to Ukraine in a rare local ceasefire. Read our liveblog to see how the events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
